//  CATALYST BED 1 of 3 -- an ADIABATIC plug-flow bed on the Dyson & Simon
//  (1968) rate law for an IRON catalyst (constant/reactions; the correlation
//  object is src/unitOperations/reactor/kinetics/AmmoniaSynthesisRate.{H,cpp}).
//  Its inlet temperature is what the FEHE delivers; its outlet temperature and
//  conversion are RESULTS.
//
//  THE VOLUME IS SOLVED AGAINST A STATED CRITERION.  The first bed is the
//  hottest: an adiabatic bed fed at ~381 C heats itself as it converts, and
//  run to a 5 K approach it would leave above the 520 C the base data give as
//  the catalyst's limit.  So bed 1 is sized to LEAVE AT 515 C (788.15 K), 5 K
//  under that limit.  The volume is `$V_Bed1`, declared in the PLANT's
//  `variables {}` (system/flowsheetDict) and SOLVED by the DesignSpec in
//  system/outerDict (Bed1.T_out = 788.15 K, simultaneously with beds 2 and
//  3).  A unit folder with no `variables {}` of its own resolves its
//  `$references` against the plant's -- until DEV.md 4c C66 it did not, and
//  this number was found by hand.  The run prints `T_out` and `approach_K`:
//  read both.

type      pfr;
operation
{
    V_R          $V_Bed1;       // catalyst bed -- SOLVED by system/outerDict; see above
    nSteps       400;           // RK4 axial steps
    thermalMode  adiabatic;     // T is a RESULT: the bed heats itself
}
reactions ( ammoniaSynthesis );
boundary  { inlets ( Feed );  outlets ( Out ); }
